# Realtime

Messages pushed to connected clients. Anything can send one, on any instance
of the API or in the worker, through the broadcaster (Redis pub/sub):

```python
from {{ name.package }}.realtime.broadcaster import EVERYONE, BroadcasterDep, user_topic


@router.post("/orders/{order_id}/ship")
async def ship(order_id: int, broadcaster: BroadcasterDep) -> None:
    ...
    await broadcaster.publish(user_topic(customer_id), "order.shipped", {"order_id": order_id})
    await broadcaster.publish(EVERYONE, "stock.changed", {"product_id": 3})
```

Every client hears `EVERYONE`; a signed-in client also hears its own
`user_topic(id)`. Each message reaches clients as `{"event", "data"}`.

